WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.640
OK, let's get into our first audience questions
for twenty twenty one very good ones, ones

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.700
I'm looking forward to answering.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:12.460
First is, David, do you think we really could
be approaching a secessions civil war scenario

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.040
after January 20th?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.470
I think that the answer is no.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:22.960
Now, if you step back and say, well, I'm going
to just focus on are there secessionist movements

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:29.290
and is there a group that would love to use
militia organization and militia power to

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.430
separate or to go against what is going to
be a Biden run federal government?

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.060
Yeah, there's no shortage of that.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.480
But the country has changed dramatically from
the times of the civil war.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.000
In the Civil War, you had two very clearly
defined factions.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.659
They were geographically much more homogenous
than what we have now, where you have even

00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:58.510
in red states, the cities are often blue,
even in blue states, the rural areas are often

00:00:58.510 --> 00:00:59.510
red.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.510
Right.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:06.050
And now it's a very urban rural situation
within states in the civil war, it was different.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:14.460
Each side had a military to back it up in
a more sort of equal way.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.670
And so right now, a lot of different things
have changed.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.530
First, there's this sort of geographical complexity.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.640
It's not clear like which states would be
part of which side.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:29.720
Urban, rural within states is the sort of
circumstance no two financial red states are

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.020
not viable without blue states.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:36.860
And we've talked a lot about when you look
at whether states pay in more or get more

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:42.120
back from the federal government, the blue
states overwhelmingly pay and more, whereas

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.740
the red states are more likely to be lechers
and receive more from the federal government.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:53.170
And absent that, a lot of those red states
would not even be financially viable.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:02:00.230
And my my guess would be, is if you see some
of these groups, militias, et cetera, escalate

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:09.629
into bombings, shootings, etc., you would
see the tide turn with police and National

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:15.209
Guard forces likely putting them down without
even getting to some kind of a more federal

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:16.209
response.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:20.280
However, I mean, like let's think ahead.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:27.209
If you imagine these red states somehow come
together and they say we're going to use our

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:30.379
combine our state National Guards, I'm speaking.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:38.629
So hypothetically, the reddest states all
together have National Guard forces of about

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:45.219
200000 troops and the federal government is
about a million and a half troops and they

00:02:45.219 --> 00:02:46.890
have all the real firepower.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:51.930
And so from a purely logistical perspective,
I'm not saying that right wing militias can't

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:52.930
cause chaos.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.709
Oh, they absolutely can.

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:55.709
They can cause chaos.

00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:56.709
They can cause death.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.079
They can do horrible, horrible things.

00:02:58.079 --> 00:03:05.610
But the circumstances are simply not ones
that would lend themselves to a true civil

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.610
war.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:13.609
And if the federal army, if the army were
to be used by the federal level to suppress

00:03:13.609 --> 00:03:19.560
this, you know, homegrown militias are not
going to be a match for the U.S. military.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.220
For better or worse, we can talk about military
industrial complex.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.629
We can talk about all of these other things.

00:03:24.629 --> 00:03:28.260
But I actually think the more interesting
topic is.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:34.109
Are there enough just people willing and interested
in that, I know that, you know, half the country

00:03:34.109 --> 00:03:37.540
or a third for 35 percent of the country didn't
vote.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:44.480
Of the people that voted for Trump, half believe
that Trump is ultimately going to be sworn

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.480
in.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.360
Some of those, when Trump is not sworn in,
might be really, really angry.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:56.819
And some subset of those might want to secede
and some subset of those might be willing

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:59.450
to actually go and fight for that in some
way.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.559
The point is, I don't think there's enough
people actually interested in that, that that

00:04:03.559 --> 00:04:06.889
you're really going to see any significant
movement along those lines.

00:04:06.889 --> 00:04:12.340
And I've talked before, we have an economic
situation that is designed to prevent people

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.079
from organizing in that way.

00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:15.709
And this is for better or worse.

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:22.770
I've talked about how cheap stuff from China
combined with easy access to credit.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:28.270
Credit cards and personal credit keeps people
relatively comfortable enough, doesn't mean

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.740
that there's no poverty, doesn't mean that
there's no hunger.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:36.420
But even people who otherwise might not like
without credit and cheap stuff from China,

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.620
there would be lots of people who on a day
to day live far worse, far less comfortably

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:42.620
than they do.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.919
So a lot of people are just going to say,
you know, I kind of would rather just hang

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:52.050
out and watch sports, not do whatever it is
the secessionists want me to do, combined

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:56.050
with the fact that due to stagnant wages and
the precarious financial situation of many

00:04:56.050 --> 00:05:01.919
people, a lot of people, you know, oh, let's
go let's go wage a civil war and try to secede,

00:05:01.919 --> 00:05:03.009
I'll be gone for two weeks.

00:05:03.009 --> 00:05:04.009
Wait a second.

00:05:04.009 --> 00:05:05.610
Then I lose health care and lose my income.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.729
And then if we don't succeed when I get back,
what do I have?

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:11.300
I lose my house, my car gets repossessed or
whatever.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.520
So that is to some degree by design in the
system that we have.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.800
And I've spoken about that before.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:23.539
So I do not expect that that is going to lead
to anything even approximating the real threat

00:05:23.539 --> 00:06:14.430
of what we might recognize as a civil war.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:07:03.550
David

